1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,180
She sold JPMorgan four million fucking customers that didn't exist.

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:10,020
Who's she? Charlie Javice, who ran Frank, a website that helped students fill out college aid forms.

3
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:14,620
You know, the giant form you need for college money? Super boring, super useful.

4
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:19,040
When banks came shopping, she said Frank had four and a quarter million users.

5
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,640
The SEC says the real number was under three hundred thousand.

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,920
That's like telling people your party had fourteen guests when one guy showed up.

7
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,000
Double-tap if you'd have fallen for it.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,300
But JPMorgan asked to see the customer list. Oops.

9
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,720
The SEC says she asked her own engineer to fake it. He refused.

10
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:42,300
So she and a coworker paid a data science professor to make up over four million fake people.

11
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,820
According to the bank's lawsuit, that cost about eighteen thousand bucks.

12
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:48,320
Send this to whoever fakes their follower count.

13
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:53,220
And it worked. JPMorgan paid one hundred seventy-five million dollars for Frank.

14
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:57,000
That's about five hundred eighty bucks for every real user. Damn.

15
00:00:57,570 --> 00:01:01,260
Then the bank tried to reach those customers, and the whole list fell apart.

16
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:03,820
Follow, 'cause the ending is chef's kiss.

17
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,580
A jury convicted her on all four counts in twenty twenty-five.

18
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:10,600
She got eighty-five months in prison, over seven years.

19
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:12,100
Prosecutors had asked for twelve.

20
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:16,500
And she was ordered to pay back two hundred eighty-seven and a half million dollars.

21
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,700
Genius or idiot? One word.

